# testsys/runlock.py's flock files, one per rotated run tree (rule 21a, item
# 70). Local, per-checkout, and meaningless in another tree: they carry the
# holding pid of a run on THIS box.
.test.lock
.test.full.lock
# Item 74: the same flock files for the two perf tools, beside the directory
# each guards -- the perf case dirs (run_perf.py, run_tpv29_pinned_compare.py)
# and the python package run_jaxmpi_ab.py stages arm files into.
testsys/perf/.perf_case.lock
testsys/perf/.perf_case_tpv29.lock
src/python/.eqdyna.lock
# Item 77: the shared case builders -- run_scaling.build_py_case (called by
# run_scaling, run_mpi_scaling, run_jaxmpi_ab, run_setup_probe and
# run_shard_scaling) and run_numa_scaling.build_case.
testsys/perf/.scaling_case.lock
testsys/perf/.numa_case.lock
# Item 81: same class, probe_plastic_traction.build_case's probe_case dir.
testsys/parity/.probe_case.lock
resume_claude.sh
.claude/
testsys/parity/evidence_output/
# Generated by testsys/perf/run_perf.py on every run, from the tracked compset.
# NEVER tracked: a committed copy of a generated case is exactly what the
# deleted parity fixtures were -- a frozen snapshot of scripts/ that drifted
# (lib.py stuck at 187 lines against the live 949) and was then exempted from
# the CI-dependency lint to keep it quiet.
testsys/perf/perf_case/
# Same reasoning, same generated-from-tracked-compset pattern, for the other
# two perf tools that build a case fresh per run (run_numa_scaling.py,
# run_scaling.py) rather than reusing run_perf.py's case dir.
testsys/perf/numa_case/
testsys/perf/scaling_case/
testsys/perf/perf_case_tpv29/
testsys/parity/probe_case/
# 484 MB of fetched submissions; the TOOLING is tracked at scripts/scec/.
# NOTE (2026-09-16, v5.8.2 audit): a trailing inline comment on this pattern's
# own line previously made the whole line -- including the comment text --
# the literal (unmatchable) gitignore pattern, so scec_archive/ was NOT
# ignored despite every doc in this repo saying it is. 693 files / ~1.16 GB
# were tracked by f2c9851 as a result. Untracked going forward in the same
# commit that fixed this pattern; the blobs remain in git history until a
# deliberate, owner-approved history rewrite (out of scope for a release).
# NOTE (2026-10-02, mira/row17-tpv2223-rebased): a SECOND leak vector, same
# shape -- a trailing slash makes a gitignore pattern match a DIRECTORY only,
# not a symlink of the same name (a worktree convenience for reusing the
# shared archive without a private copy). `scec_archive/` left a `scec_archive
# -> <repo>/EQdyna/scec_archive` symlink in this worktree genuinely
# UNIGNORED (`git check-ignore` confirmed it), one `git add -A` away from
# tracking a symlink that resolves outside this worktree entirely. Dropped
# the trailing slash so the pattern matches the symlink too.
scec_archive
relnotes_v*.md
# testsys/perf/elem_scaling_last.json tracked: raw evidence behind measured_runs.md
# (its harness was removed 2026-09-15 -- see that file's header)
*.provenance
# mkdocs build output (docs/user/mkdocs.yml's site_dir) -- a byproduct, never
# tracked (rule 12).
docs/user-site/
# eqdyna_sweep_* used to land at repo root (PR #52); it and run.py's own
# console log now land under test/ or test.prev/ instead (owner, 2026-09-29:
# logs live with the run, same place on every machine), both already
# ignored wholesale above.

# Repo tidy 2026-10-09 (item 3, owner amendment: "most md no need to go out,
# they in the end in release notes already"): the ~30 root-level
# docs/NOTES_*.md / docs/SESSION_LOG_*.md dev notes were removed from the
# tracked tree (content already summarised in docs/pastReleaseNotes.md;
# git history keeps the old files, nothing was rewritten). A new one of
# either shape stays local from here on rather than landing at the root of
# docs/ again; docs/notes/ (the earlier, already-consolidated batch) is
# untouched by this pattern.
docs/NOTES_*.md
docs/SESSION_LOG_*.md
